WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.520
Let's go next to Ivan from Phenix, Arizona.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.439
Ivan, you're on the air.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.740
Hi, David.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.320
How are you?

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.320
Good.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:17.029
So I'm currently a senior in high school,
and recently I've been paying attention to

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:19.099
the local elections over here.

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:24.609
And I'm actually in Goa, but like also the
politicians here.

00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:30.350
And I've realized that, like a lot of them
are extremely slimy people.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:35.100
I'm just curious how I can get more involved
to make sure that these types of people aren't

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.000
elected anymore, especially as Arizona is
becoming more left leaning.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.600
Yeah, I mean, you know, pay attention to whether
there is a candidate that you find to be not

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.580
slimy that runs at the city council level,
mayoral level, whatever, and work for their

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.580
campaign.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.040
I mean, there's no all of these upstart campaigns
want volunteers.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.280
And if you don't see anybody who you want
to put your efforts behind, consider maybe

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.860
running yourself at some point.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.989
But that's this is exactly the right question.

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:08.329
You don't like the people that are representing
you.

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:10.590
And so you have you can have a voice in that.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:14.119
And that means not only can you will you be
able to vote, I don't know if you're already

00:01:14.119 --> 00:01:15.250
old enough to vote.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.039
Not only will you be able to vote, but you
can run.

00:01:18.039 --> 00:01:19.710
You can support other candidates.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:23.340
You can draft other candidates and say to
someone, you should really run against this

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.340
person.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:28.170
So, yeah, the local level is where you can
actually have the biggest and fastest impact

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.170
in many ways.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.560
Yeah, that's what I was thinking last year.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:38.299
I had the opportunity to go to the Capitol
for like an environmental day and speak with

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:43.040
the my my representative.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.280
And he just started questioning like this.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.369
Sources are biology books came from.

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:49.020
Oh my God.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.020
Yeah.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.509
It was like an absolute mess.

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:56.590
So I just want to make sure, like, these types
of people aren't able to have any power.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:02.330
You know, I just recently was reading that
the the most dangerous state to be in from

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.250
the standpoint of the pandemic is Arizona.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.250
Have you.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.310
Does that resonate with you in terms of what
you've seen?

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.409
Oh, yeah.

00:02:09.409 --> 00:02:12.159
It's a complete mess here.

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:15.770
People don't wear masks in stores like I work
at a Wal-Mart.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:22.290
And probably one third of the people aren't
wearing masks when they're inside schools.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.180
Nobody wears masks.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.939
It's it's just really bad here.

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:28.240
And how about as far as vaccines?

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.950
Are you hearing a lot of anti vaccine talk?

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:37.080
I'm actually I haven't heard too much anti
vax talk, just more so people still believing

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.190
that the virus is just a Democratic hoax.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:45.379
Well, the weird thing about that is you'd
think that it would have ended when Joe Biden

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:46.379
was sworn in.

00:02:46.379 --> 00:02:52.900
Yeah, I mean, I my my uncle kept saying that
come November 3rd, the coronavirus is going

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:53.900
to be over.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:54.900
Right.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:55.920
Look, here we are.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.599
Have you talked to him and asked what happened?

00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:01.340
I haven't actually.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.500
We don't have the strongest relation.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.569
OK, yeah, I can guess why.

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:07.569
Yeah.

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:08.569
All right.

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:10.920
Well, listen, Ivan, you're asking all the
right questions.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.360
You're doing all the right things.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.360
It's great that you're involved.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.870
Well, thank you very much, David.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.410
All right, Ivan from Phenix.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:23.340
Fantastic, fantastic to have young folks involved.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.939
Very, very important.

